# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Pengenalan {#introduction}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a chemist runs an NMR experiment, they place a sample of nuclear spins in a strong magnetic field, apply a radio-frequency (RF) pulse, and measure the signal that comes back. The technique rests on a few ideas from the quantum mechanics of a spin-1/2 particle in a magnetic field. The spin has two energy levels separated by an energy that corresponds to a characteristic Larmor frequency. A resonant pulse at that frequency tips the spin into the transverse plane, where it precesses and induces a signal that then fades with two characteristic times, $T_1$ and $T_2$.\n"
msgstr "Apabila ahli kimia menjalankan eksperimen NMR, mereka meletakkan sampel spin nuklear dalam medan magnet yang kuat, menggunakan denyutan frekuensi radio (RF), dan mengukur isyarat yang kembali. Teknik ini berasaskan beberapa idea daripada mekanik kuantum bagi zarah spin-1/2 dalam medan magnet. Spin itu mempunyai dua aras tenaga yang dipisahkan oleh tenaga yang sepadan dengan frekuensi Larmor yang tertentu. Denyutan resonans pada frekuensi itu mengalihkan spin ke satah melintang, di mana ia berpusing dan mengaruh isyarat yang kemudian pudar dengan dua masa tertentu, $T_1$ dan $T_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A superconducting **qubit** is an engineered version of the same object: a controllable two-level quantum system. Its $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ states are the analog of spin-up and spin-down, the gate we apply to rotate it is the analog of the RF pulse, and it loses coherence with its own $T_1$ and $T_2$. This is not merely a loose comparison; some of the earliest experimental quantum processors in the late 1990s and early 2000s used NMR.\n"
msgstr "**Qubit** superkonduktor ialah versi kejuruteraan bagi objek yang sama: sistem kuantum dua aras yang boleh dikawal. Keadaan $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$ adalah analog spin-atas dan spin-bawah, gate yang kita gunakan untuk memutarkannya adalah analog denyutan RF, dan ia kehilangan koheren dengan $T_1$ dan $T_2$ tersendiri. Ini bukan sekadar perbandingan longgar; sesetengah pemproses kuantum eksperimen terawal pada penghujung 1990-an dan awal 2000-an menggunakan NMR.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this module you will use a real quantum computer to run the same characterization experiments that an NMR spectroscopist (or a quantum engineer calibrating hardware) performs:\n"
msgstr "Dalam modul ini anda akan menggunakan komputer kuantum sebenar untuk menjalankan eksperimen pencirian yang sama seperti yang dilakukan oleh ahli spektroskopi NMR (atau jurutera kuantum yang menentukur perkakasan):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Rabi / nutation** — driving the spin and watching it rotate. This is how you calibrate a $\\pi$ or $\\pi/2$ rotation.\n"
msgstr "**Rabi / nutasi** — memacu spin dan melihatnya berputar. Beginilah cara anda menentukur putaran $\\pi$ atau $\\pi/2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_1$** — spin-lattice relaxation, the decay of an excited spin back to equilibrium.\n"
msgstr "**$T_1$** — relaksasi spin-kekisi, pereputan spin teruja kembali ke keseimbangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_2$** — spin-spin relaxation (dephasing), measured with a Ramsey experiment and refocused with a Hahn echo.\n"
msgstr "**$T_2$** — relaksasi spin-spin (nyahfasa), diukur dengan eksperimen Ramsey dan difokus semula dengan gema Hahn.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NMR spectroscopy (chemical shift and $J$-coupling)** — simulating a small molecule on several qubits and reading its multiplet spectrum to recover connectivity through the $n+1$ rule.\n"
msgstr "**Spektroskopi NMR (anjakan kimia dan gandingan $J$)** — mensimulasikan molekul kecil pada beberapa qubit dan membaca spektrum multipletnya untuk memulihkan kesambungan melalui peraturan $n+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each concept we first give the minimal theory, then implement the experiment in Qiskit following the four-step *Qiskit patterns* workflow.\n"
msgstr "Bagi setiap konsep, kita mula-mula memberikan teori minimum, kemudian melaksanakan eksperimen dalam Qiskit mengikut aliran kerja *Qiskit patterns* empat langkah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory}"
msgstr "Teori {#theory}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-1/2 particles in a magnetic field {#spin-12-particles-in-a-magnetic-field}"
msgstr "Zarah spin-1/2 dalam medan magnet {#spin-12-particles-in-a-magnetic-field}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A spin-1/2 nucleus has a magnetic moment $\\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\gamma \\hbar \\mathbf{I}$, where $\\gamma$ is the gyromagnetic ratio. In a static field $B_0$ along $z$, the two spin states split in energy (the **Zeeman effect**):\n"
msgstr "Nukleus spin-1/2 mempunyai momen magnet $\\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\gamma \\hbar \\mathbf{I}$, dengan $\\gamma$ ialah nisbah giromagnet. Dalam medan statik $B_0$ sepanjang $z$, dua keadaan spin berpecah dari segi tenaga (**kesan Zeeman**):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$E_{\\pm} = \\mp \\tfrac{1}{2}\\gamma \\hbar B_0, \\qquad \\Delta E = \\gamma \\hbar B_0 = \\hbar \\omega_0 .$$\n"
msgstr "$$E_{\\pm} = \\mp \\tfrac{1}{2}\\gamma \\hbar B_0, \\qquad \\Delta E = \\gamma \\hbar B_0 = \\hbar \\omega_0 .$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The energy gap defines the **Larmor (resonance) frequency** $\\omega_0 = \\gamma B_0$. The magnetic moment **precesses** about $B_0$ at this same frequency.\n"
msgstr "Jurang tenaga mentakrifkan **frekuensi Larmor (resonans)** $\\omega_0 = \\gamma B_0$. Momen magnet **berpusing** mengelilingi $B_0$ pada frekuensi yang sama ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To rotate the spin we apply an oscillating RF field at (or near) $\\omega_0$. In the frame rotating at the drive frequency (the **rotating frame**), a resonant drive rotates the Bloch vector about an axis in the $x$-$y$ plane. How far it rotates (the **flip angle**) is set by the pulse's strength and duration. Two choices matter most: a $90^\\circ$ pulse tips a $+1/2$ spin into the transverse plane, and a $180^\\circ$ pulse rotates it fully to $-1/2$.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memutarkan spin kita menggunakan medan RF berayun pada (atau berhampiran) $\\omega_0$. Dalam bingkai yang berputar pada frekuensi pemacu (**bingkai berputar**), pemacu resonans memutarkan vektor Bloch mengelilingi paksi dalam satah $x$-$y$. Sejauh mana ia berputar (**sudut selak**) ditentukan oleh kekuatan dan tempoh denyutan. Dua pilihan paling penting: denyutan $90^\\circ$ mengalihkan spin $+1/2$ ke satah melintang, dan denyutan $180^\\circ$ memutarkannya sepenuhnya ke $-1/2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Translating between NMR and quantum computing jargon {#translating-between-nmr-and-quantum-computing-jargon}"
msgstr "Menterjemah antara jargon NMR dan pengkomputeran kuantum {#translating-between-nmr-and-quantum-computing-jargon}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit is a two-level system, mathematically identical to a spin-1/2 in a magnetic field &mdash; so while we're running on a quantum processor rather than a nucleus, the physics is the same physics that underlies NMR. Only the vocabulary differs. This table helps you talk to physical chemists and quantum-computing specialists alike.\n"
msgstr "Qubit ialah sistem dua aras, secara matematik serupa dengan spin-1/2 dalam medan magnet &mdash; jadi walaupun kita berjalan pada pemproses kuantum dan bukan nukleus, fizik yang mendasari NMR adalah fizik yang sama. Hanya perbendaharaan katanya berbeza. Jadual ini membantu anda berbual dengan ahli kimia fizik dan pakar pengkomputeran kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| NMR / spin-1/2 | Quantum processor (qubit) |\n"
"| ---|---|\n"
"| Spin-up / spin-down | $\\ket{0}$ / $\\ket{1}$ |\n"
"| Zeeman gap $\\Delta E = \\hbar\\omega_0$ | Qubit transition energy $\\hbar\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Larmor frequency $\\omega_0$ | Qubit frequency $\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Resonant RF pulse (flip angle $\\theta$) | Single-qubit rotation gate $R_X(\\theta)$ |\n"
"| $90^\\circ$ / $180^\\circ$ pulse | $R_X(\\pi/2)$ / $R_X(\\pi)$ |\n"
"| Spin-lattice relaxation $T_1$ | Qubit energy-relaxation time $T_1$ |\n"
"| Spin-spin relaxation $T_2$ | Qubit dephasing time $T_2$ |\n"
"| Nutation | Rabi oscillations |\n"
"| Free induction decay (FID), Hahn echo | Ramsey, echo sequences |\n"
msgstr ""
"| NMR / spin-1/2 | Pemproses kuantum (qubit) |\n"
"| ---|---|\n"
"| Spin-atas / spin-bawah | $\\ket{0}$ / $\\ket{1}$ |\n"
"| Jurang Zeeman $\\Delta E = \\hbar\\omega_0$ | Tenaga peralihan qubit $\\hbar\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Frekuensi Larmor $\\omega_0$ | Frekuensi qubit $\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Denyutan RF resonans (sudut selak $\\theta$) | Gate putaran qubit tunggal $R_X(\\theta)$ |\n"
"| Denyutan $90^\\circ$ / $180^\\circ$ | $R_X(\\pi/2)$ / $R_X(\\pi)$ |\n"
"| Relaksasi spin-kekisi $T_1$ | Masa relaksasi tenaga qubit $T_1$ |\n"
"| Relaksasi spin-spin $T_2$ | Masa nyahfasa qubit $T_2$ |\n"
"| Nutasi | Ayunan Rabi |\n"
"| Pereputan induksi bebas (FID), gema Hahn | Jujukan Ramsey, gema |\n"

