# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experiment: Rabi oscillations (nutation) {#experiment-rabi-oscillations-nutation}"
msgstr "Eksperimen: ayunan Rabi (nutasi) {#experiment-rabi-oscillations-nutation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory-1}"
msgstr "Teori {#theory-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drive a spin on resonance and its Bloch vector rotates steadily from pole to pole &mdash; it **nutates**. If we apply a rotation of flip angle $\\theta$ about the $x$-axis to a qubit starting in $|0\\rangle$, the probability of finding it in $|1\\rangle$ is:\n"
msgstr "Pacu spin pada resonans dan vektor Blochnya berputar dengan stabil dari kutub ke kutub &mdash; ia **bernutasi**. Jika kita menggunakan putaran dengan sudut selak $\\theta$ mengelilingi paksi-$x$ pada qubit yang bermula dalam $|0\\rangle$, kebarangkalian mendapatinya dalam $|1\\rangle$ ialah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$P_1(\\theta) = \\sin^2\\!\\left(\\tfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\bigl(1 - \\cos\\theta\\bigr).$$\n"
msgstr "$$P_1(\\theta) = \\sin^2\\!\\left(\\tfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\bigl(1 - \\cos\\theta\\bigr).$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the **Rabi curve**. Its first maximum is the $\\pi$ pulse (full inversion, the $180^\\circ$ pulse); a $\\pi/2$ pulse is a quarter-turn (the $90^\\circ$ pulse that tips a spin into the transverse plane). In NMR this curve is how you *calibrate* your pulses.\n"
msgstr "Ini ialah **lengkung Rabi**. Maksimum pertamanya ialah denyutan $\\pi$ (penyongsangan penuh, denyutan $180^\\circ$); denyutan $\\pi/2$ ialah suku pusingan (denyutan $90^\\circ$ yang mengalihkan spin ke satah melintang). Dalam NMR, lengkung ini ialah cara anda *menentukur* denyutan anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Experimental caveat\">\n"
"A *literal* Rabi experiment sweeps the drive amplitude or duration in time. That requires pulse-level control, which was removed in Qiskit v2.0. Here we instead sweep the **rotation angle** $\\theta$ of an $R_X(\\theta)$ gate. The curve and the $\\pi$/$\\pi/2$ identification are identical; the only difference is that we choose an angle directly instead of calibrating a pulse length. On hardware with *fractional gates*, $R_X(\\theta)$ for arbitrary $\\theta$ runs natively.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Kaveat eksperimen\">\n"
"Eksperimen Rabi *literal* menyapu amplitud atau tempoh pemacu dalam masa. Itu memerlukan kawalan aras denyutan, yang telah dialih keluar dalam Qiskit v2.0. Di sini kita sebaliknya menyapu **sudut putaran** $\\theta$ bagi gate $R_X(\\theta)$. Lengkung dan pengenalpastian $\\pi$/$\\pi/2$ adalah serupa; satu-satunya perbezaan ialah kita memilih sudut secara langsung dan bukan menentukur tempoh denyutan. Pada perkakasan dengan *gate pecahan*, $R_X(\\theta)$ untuk $\\theta$ sewenang-wenangnya dijalankan secara natif.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
