# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experiment: $T_2$, $T_2^*$ {#experiment-t-2-t-2}"
msgstr "Eksperimen: $T_2$, $T_2^*$ {#experiment-t-2-t-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory-3}"
msgstr "Teori {#theory-3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$T_1$ measures *energy* loss. $T_2$ measures loss of **phase coherence** in the transverse plane. We can observe this with a **Ramsey experiment**: a $\\pi/2$ pulse rotates all the spins down to the equator, all pointing in the same direction. They Larmor precess, but each one precesses at a slightly different frequency, so they fan out along the equator and the net transverse signal decays, with a characteristic decay time of $T_2^*$.\n"
msgstr "$T_1$ mengukur kehilangan *tenaga*. $T_2$ mengukur kehilangan **koheren fasa** dalam satah melintang. Kita boleh memerhatikannya dengan **eksperimen Ramsey**: denyut $\\pi/2$ memutar semua spin ke bawah sehingga khatulistiwa, semuanya menuju arah yang sama. Ia berpresesi Larmor, tetapi setiap satu berpresesi pada frekuensi yang sedikit berbeza, jadi ia terkembang di sepanjang khatulistiwa dan isyarat melintang bersih mereput, dengan masa pereputan ciri $T_2^*$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Aside for quantum readers:** The fanning-out picture shows one way to lose coherence: a spread of definite phases that average out. It's worth knowing this isn't the only mechanism. Coherence can also be lost because the phase becomes entangled with the environment, so it's no longer a definite value the system holds at all. You can't tell the two mechanisms apart just by watching the signal decay, so the fanning-out picture is a good intuition. Be mindful not to read it as the complete or literal story.\n"
msgstr "**Catatan sampingan untuk pembaca kuantum:** Gambaran terkembang ini menunjukkan satu cara kehilangan koheren: serakan fasa tertentu yang saling memurnikan. Perlu diketahui bahawa ini bukan satu-satunya mekanisme. Koheren juga boleh hilang kerana fasa menjadi terkait (entangled) dengan persekitaran, jadi ia bukan lagi nilai tertentu yang dipegang oleh sistem sama sekali. Anda tidak dapat membezakan kedua-dua mekanisme itu hanya dengan memerhatikan pereputan isyarat, jadi gambaran terkembang ini ialah intuisi yang baik. Berhati-hatilah supaya tidak menganggapnya sebagai cerita yang lengkap atau literal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two effects dephase a spin:\n"
"* Irreversible (or effectively irreversible) decoherence arising from uncontrolled coupling to other degrees of freedom, characterized by the true $T_2$. In NMR, this generally comes from molecular motion modulating the couplings between spins. In quantum computing, it corresponds to unwanted couplings between qubits and the environment.\n"
"* Static or slowly-varying, reversible frequency offsets, such as field inhomogeneity, qubit-to-qubit frequency variation, and calibration errors. Combined with the true $T_2$, these produce the shorter apparent decay time $T_2^*$ observed in a Ramsey experiment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua kesan menyebabkan spin hilang fasa:\n"
"* Dekoheren tak boleh balik (atau secara berkesan tak boleh balik) yang timbul daripada gandingan tidak terkawal dengan darjah kebebasan lain, dicirikan oleh $T_2$ sebenar. Dalam NMR, ini umumnya datang daripada gerakan molekul yang memodulasi gandingan antara spin. Dalam pengkomputeran kuantum, ia sepadan dengan gandingan tidak diingini antara qubit dan persekitaran.\n"
"* Ofset frekuensi statik atau berubah perlahan yang boleh balik, seperti ketakhomogenan medan, variasi frekuensi antara qubit, dan ralat penentukuran. Digabungkan dengan $T_2$ sebenar, ini menghasilkan masa pereputan ketara yang lebih pendek $T_2^*$ yang diperhatikan dalam eksperimen Ramsey.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So how do we recover the true $T_2$ if a Ramsey experiment only tells us about $T_2^*$? The second experiment, called a **Hahn echo**, cancels all the noise of the second type to find the true $T_2$. It starts the same as a Ramsey experiment, with a $\\pi/2$ pulse, then the spins fan out as before. After some time $\\tau$, a $\\pi$ pulse is applied. The pulse reverses the phase accumulation caused by static frequency offsets, so the spins refocus after a second delay of the same duration, $\\tau$.\n"
msgstr "Jadi bagaimanakah kita memulihkan $T_2$ sebenar jika eksperimen Ramsey hanya memberitahu kita tentang $T_2^*$? Eksperimen kedua, yang dipanggil **gema Hahn**, membatalkan semua hingar jenis kedua untuk mendapatkan $T_2$ sebenar. Ia bermula sama seperti eksperimen Ramsey, dengan denyut $\\pi/2$, kemudian spin terkembang seperti sebelumnya. Selepas beberapa masa $\\tau$, denyut $\\pi$ dikenakan. Denyut itu membalikkan pengumpulan fasa yang disebabkan oleh ofset frekuensi statik, jadi spin memfokus semula selepas kelewatan kedua yang sama tempohnya, $\\tau$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$T_2^*$ and $T_2$ are both important numbers to know in both the chemistry setting and the quantum computing setting. In the chemistry setting, $T_2^*$ sets your linewidth for a standard NMR experiment (you'll see what this means in a later [section](#nmr-spectroscopy)). $T_2$ can tell you much about the molecules, such as molecular tumbling, and a change in $T_2$ can signal that a molecule has bound to something larger. In the quantum computing setting, we generally want both $T_2$ and $T_2^*$ to be as long as possible, so we have more time to perform experiments before decoherence overwhelms the system. A whole family of techniques based on the Hahn echo extends this time by canceling the reversible noise, so that the circuit is ideally limited by the true $T_2$, not $T_2^*$. This is called \"dynamical decoupling.\"\n"
msgstr "$T_2^*$ dan $T_2$ kedua-duanya nombor penting untuk diketahui dalam tetapan kimia dan tetapan pengkomputeran kuantum. Dalam tetapan kimia, $T_2^*$ menentukan lebar garis bagi eksperimen NMR piawai (anda akan melihat maksudnya dalam [bahagian](#nmr-spectroscopy) kemudian). $T_2$ boleh memberitahu banyak perkara tentang molekul, seperti jungkir-balik molekul, dan perubahan dalam $T_2$ boleh menandakan bahawa molekul telah terikat pada sesuatu yang lebih besar. Dalam tetapan pengkomputeran kuantum, kita umumnya mahu $T_2$ dan $T_2^*$ sepanjang yang mungkin, supaya kita mempunyai lebih banyak masa untuk menjalankan eksperimen sebelum dekoheren menguasai sistem. Satu keluarga teknik berasaskan gema Hahn melanjutkan masa ini dengan membatalkan hingar boleh balik, supaya litar secara ideal dihadkan oleh $T_2$ sebenar, bukan $T_2^*$. Ini dipanggil \"penyahgandingan dinamik.\"\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation {#implementation}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan {#implementation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When we implement the Ramsey and Hahn echo experiments on a qubit, the readout is slightly different than for the NMR case. In NMR, you can directly observe the oscillating fields induced by the spins precessing at the Larmor frequency in the transverse plane. But with a qubit, we can only measure its projection along the $Z$ axis, that is, whether it's $\\vert 0 \\rangle$ or $\\vert 1 \\rangle$. Therefore, for both experiments, we end with an additional $\\pi/2$ pulse followed by a measurement. This $\\pi/2$ pulse translates the phase information of the qubit into a population.\n"
msgstr "Apabila kita melaksanakan eksperimen Ramsey dan gema Hahn pada qubit, bacaan sedikit berbeza daripada kes NMR. Dalam NMR, anda boleh memerhatikan terus medan berayun yang teraruh oleh spin yang berpresesi pada frekuensi Larmor dalam satah melintang. Tetapi dengan qubit, kita hanya dapat mengukur unjurannya sepanjang paksi $Z$, iaitu sama ada ia $\\vert 0 \\rangle$ atau $\\vert 1 \\rangle$. Oleh itu, bagi kedua-dua eksperimen, kita menamatkan dengan denyut $\\pi/2$ tambahan diikuti pengukuran. Denyut $\\pi/2$ ini menukar maklumat fasa qubit menjadi populasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below we run each experiment to determine $T_2^*$ and $T_2$.\n"
msgstr "Di bawah, kita menjalankan setiap eksperimen untuk menentukan $T_2^*$ dan $T_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ramsey ($T_2^{*}$): Two $\\pi/2$ pulses with delay time $\\tau$ {#ramsey-t-2-two-pi2-pulses-with-delay-time-tau}"
msgstr "Ramsey ($T_2^{*}$): Dua denyut $\\pi/2$ dengan masa kelewatan $\\tau$ {#ramsey-t-2-two-pi2-pulses-with-delay-time-tau}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first $\\pi/2$ pulse tips the Bloch vector to the equator, and the next one translates the phase of the Bloch vector to a population. Because the phase changes in time as the Bloch vector precesses, we see a sinusoidal pattern in the population as a function of precession time $\\tau$. As the qubit loses phase coherence we should see the amplitude of this sine curve decay.\n"
msgstr "Denyut $\\pi/2$ pertama mencondongkan vektor Bloch ke khatulistiwa, dan yang seterusnya menukar fasa vektor Bloch menjadi populasi. Oleh kerana fasa berubah mengikut masa apabila vektor Bloch berpresesi, kita melihat corak sinusoid dalam populasi sebagai fungsi masa presesi $\\tau$. Apabila qubit kehilangan koheren fasa, kita sepatutnya melihat amplitud lengkung sinus ini mereput.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Some more subtleties for the quantum readers:** In quantum computing experiments, the oscillations we see aren't actually at the Larmor frequency, which is in the GHz range and much too fast for us to resolve. Quantum experiments operate in the *rotating frame*: a frame that spins along with the qubit at (near) the Larmor frequency, so the fast precession is invisible and the Bloch vector looks nearly still. To see fringes, we deliberately set our rotating frame slightly detuned from the Larmor frequency. The Bloch vector then appears to precess at that small detuning, and we get an oscillating signal at the detuning frequency. Below, we don't fix the detuning at one value; we choose it so that about a dozen fringes span the measurement window (which we size to the qubit's coherence time), which keeps the oscillation easy to sample without aliasing. One more wrinkle: in Qiskit we don't have the pulse-level control needed to change the pulse frequency (which is what sets the rotating-frame frequency). Instead, we add an *effective* detuning by hand, using it to set the phase of the second Ramsey pulse. It's a bit contrived, but the result is the same and the decay we observe is still the genuine $T_2^*$.\n"
msgstr "**Beberapa kehalusan lagi untuk pembaca kuantum:** Dalam eksperimen pengkomputeran kuantum, ayunan yang kita lihat sebenarnya bukan pada frekuensi Larmor, yang berada dalam julat GHz dan terlalu pantas untuk kita bezakan. Eksperimen kuantum beroperasi dalam *bingkai berputar*: bingkai yang berputar bersama qubit pada (hampir) frekuensi Larmor, jadi presesi pantas itu tidak kelihatan dan vektor Bloch kelihatan hampir pegun. Untuk melihat pinggir, kita sengaja menetapkan bingkai berputar kita sedikit menyimpang daripada frekuensi Larmor. Vektor Bloch kemudian kelihatan berpresesi pada sisihan kecil itu, dan kita mendapat isyarat berayun pada frekuensi sisihan. Di bawah, kita tidak menetapkan sisihan pada satu nilai; kita memilihnya supaya kira-kira sedozen pinggir merangkumi tetingkap pengukuran (yang saiznya kita sesuaikan dengan masa koheren qubit), yang memastikan ayunan mudah disampel tanpa aliasing. Satu lagi kerumitan: dalam Qiskit kita tidak mempunyai kawalan aras denyut yang diperlukan untuk menukar frekuensi denyut (yang menetapkan frekuensi bingkai berputar). Sebaliknya, kita menambah sisihan *berkesan* secara manual, menggunakannya untuk menetapkan fasa denyut Ramsey kedua. Ia agak dibuat-buat, tetapi hasilnya sama dan pereputan yang kita perhatikan masih $T_2^*$ yang tulen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Bloch-sphere view {#a-bloch-sphere-view-2}"
msgstr "Pandangan sfera Bloch {#a-bloch-sphere-view-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A $\\pi/2$ pulse tips the spins to the equator; each then precesses at a slightly different rate and they **fan out**, so the net (red) vector shrinks as they dephase — this decay is $T_2^*$.\n"
msgstr "Denyut $\\pi/2$ mencondongkan spin ke khatulistiwa; setiap satu kemudian berpresesi pada kadar yang sedikit berbeza dan ia **terkembang**, jadi vektor bersih (merah) mengecil apabila ia hilang fasa — pereputan ini ialah $T_2^*$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<IBMVideo id=\"135063680\" title=\"Bloch-sphere animation of T2-star dephasing and loss of net transverse magnetization.\"/>\n"
msgstr "<IBMVideo id=\"135063680\" title=\"Animasi sfera Bloch bagi kehilangan fasa T2-bintang dan kehilangan magnetisasi melintang bersih.\"/>\n"

