msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read each question, think about your answer, then click the triangle to reveal the solution.\n"
msgstr "Baca setiap soalan, fikirkan jawapan anda, kemudian klik segi tiga untuk mendedahkan penyelesaian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the AX spectrum the two doublets are separated (center-to-center) by 12 Hz, and the two lines within each doublet are 2 Hz apart. Which number is the chemical-shift difference and which is the coupling constant $J$? If you moved to a spectrometer with twice the magnetic field, which one would change?\n"
msgstr "Dalam spektrum AX, kedua-dua doublet dipisahkan (pusat ke pusat) sebanyak 12 Hz, dan dua garis dalam setiap doublet berjarak 2 Hz. Nombor manakah perbezaan anjakan kimia dan yang manakah pemalar gandingan $J$? Jika anda beralih kepada spektrometer dengan medan magnet dua kali ganda, yang manakah akan berubah?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 12 Hz center-to-center separation is the **chemical-shift difference** ($\\nu_1-\\nu_2$); the 2 Hz line spacing is the **coupling constant $J$**. Chemical shifts come from shielding of $B_0$, so they scale with the field. At twice the field the separation doubles to 24 Hz. The coupling $J$ is a through-bond molecular property and is field-independent, so it stays 2 Hz. Chemists tell shift from coupling by watching how a splitting scales with field.\n"
msgstr "Pemisahan pusat ke pusat 12 Hz ialah **perbezaan anjakan kimia** ($\\nu_1-\\nu_2$); jarak garis 2 Hz ialah **pemalar gandingan $J$**. Anjakan kimia datang daripada perlindungan $B_0$, jadi ia berskala dengan medan. Pada medan dua kali ganda, pemisahan menjadi dua kali ganda kepada 24 Hz. Gandingan $J$ ialah sifat molekul melalui ikatan dan tidak bergantung pada medan, jadi ia kekal 2 Hz. Ahli kimia membezakan anjakan daripada gandingan dengan memerhatikan bagaimana pemecahan berskala dengan medan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the $n+1$ rule, predict the A multiplet if a *third* equivalent X spin were added (an AX$_3$ system), and explain why the two equivalent X spins in AX$_2$ produce no splitting of each other.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan peraturan $n+1$, ramalkan multiplet A jika spin X setara *ketiga* ditambah (sistem AX$_3$), dan jelaskan mengapa dua spin X setara dalam AX$_2$ tidak memecahkan satu sama lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
"With $n=3$ equivalent neighbors, A becomes a 1:3:3:1 quartet. Equivalent spins don't split each other because their coupling shifts the relevant energy levels all by the same amount, so the gaps between those levels &mdash; the frequencies we see &mdash; don't change.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Jawapan\">\n"
"Dengan $n=3$ jiran setara, A menjadi kuartet 1:3:3:1. Spin setara tidak memecahkan satu sama lain kerana gandingan mereka menganjak aras tenaga yang berkaitan dengan jumlah yang sama, jadi jurang antara aras itu &mdash; frekuensi yang kita lihat &mdash; tidak berubah.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

