# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have used a real quantum computer to explore how nuclear spins precess and decohere in an NMR experiment, and how to interpret the resulting spectra. It's worth stepping back to review why this was possible at all, and why it's more than a curiosity.\n"
msgstr "Kita telah menggunakan komputer kuantum sebenar untuk meneroka bagaimana spin nuklear berpresesi dan mengalami dekoheren dalam eksperimen NMR, dan bagaimana mentafsir spektrum yang terhasil. Wajar untuk berundur sebentar dan menilai mengapa ini boleh dilakukan sama sekali, dan mengapa ia lebih daripada sekadar keganjilan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit and a spin-1/2 nucleus are, mathematically, the same object: two-level quantum systems living on the Bloch sphere, rotated by resonant pulses, precessing about an axis, and losing coherence to their surroundings. The entire vocabulary of this module (the Larmor frequency, the rotating frame, $T_1$, $T_2$, and $T_2^*$, Ramsey fringes, the Hahn echo) belongs to NMR and quantum computing equally. What a chemist calls a *chemical shift*, a quantum engineer calls a *single-qubit $Z$ rotation*; what a chemist calls a *$J$-coupling*, a quantum engineer calls a *$ZZ$ interaction*. The two fields have been describing the same physics in different words.\n"
msgstr "Qubit dan nukleus spin-1/2 secara matematik ialah objek yang sama: sistem kuantum dua aras yang hidup pada sfera Bloch, diputar oleh denyut resonan, berpresesi pada satu paksi, dan kehilangan koheren kepada persekitarannya. Keseluruhan perbendaharaan kata modul ini (frekuensi Larmor, bingkai berputar, $T_1$, $T_2$, dan $T_2^*$, pinggir Ramsey, gema Hahn) menjadi milik NMR dan pengkomputeran kuantum sama rata. Apa yang ahli kimia panggil *anjakan kimia*, jurutera kuantum panggil *putaran $Z$ satu qubit*; apa yang ahli kimia panggil *gandingan $J$*, jurutera kuantum panggil *interaksi $ZZ$*. Kedua-dua bidang telah menerangkan fizik yang sama dalam perkataan yang berbeza.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That connection is historical, not just conceptual: NMR was one of the first platforms to run real quantum algorithms. By 2001, a molecule in solution had executed Shor's algorithm to factor 15, with each nuclear spin serving as a qubit. NMR also handed quantum computing much of its control toolkit. The spin echo, CPMG pulse trains, composite pulses, and dynamical decoupling were all invented by spectroscopists decades before qubits needed them to fight decoherence. There is a satisfying symmetry in what we just did: the field that gave birth to early quantum computers is now something a quantum computer can simulate.\n"
msgstr "Kaitan itu bersifat sejarah, bukan sekadar konseptual: NMR ialah salah satu platform pertama yang menjalankan algoritma kuantum sebenar. Menjelang 2001, sebuah molekul dalam larutan telah melaksanakan algoritma Shor untuk memfaktorkan 15, dengan setiap spin nuklear berfungsi sebagai qubit. NMR juga menyumbangkan banyak kit alat kawalannya kepada pengkomputeran kuantum. Gema spin, rentetan denyut CPMG, denyut komposit, dan penyahgandingan dinamik semuanya dicipta oleh ahli spektroskopi beberapa dekad sebelum qubit memerlukannya untuk melawan dekoheren. Terdapat simetri yang memuaskan dalam apa yang baru kita lakukan: bidang yang melahirkan komputer kuantum awal kini menjadi sesuatu yang boleh disimulasikan oleh komputer kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Review and questions {#review-and-questions}"
msgstr "Ulang kaji dan soalan {#review-and-questions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Konsep kritikal {#critical-concepts}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit is an engineered two-level system equivalent to a spin-1/2; its $|0\\rangle/|1\\rangle$, frequency, gates, $T_1$, and $T_2$ are the direct analogs of NMR quantities.\n"
msgstr "Qubit ialah sistem dua aras kejuruteraan yang setara dengan spin-1/2; $|0\\rangle/|1\\rangle$, frekuensi, get, $T_1$, dan $T_2$ nya ialah analog langsung kuantiti NMR.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A resonant pulse rotates the Bloch vector; the flip angle sets the rotation, and the Rabi/nutation curve $P_1=\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$ identifies $\\pi$ and $\\pi/2$ rotations.\n"
msgstr "Denyut resonan memutar vektor Bloch; sudut kilas menentukan putaran, dan lengkung Rabi/nutasi $P_1=\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$ mengenal pasti putaran $\\pi$ dan $\\pi/2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$T_1$ is energy (spin-lattice) relaxation; $T_2$ is phase (spin-spin) relaxation; $T_2^{*}$ additionally includes reversible static dephasing that a Hahn echo refocuses.\n"
msgstr "$T_1$ ialah relaksasi tenaga (spin-kekisi); $T_2$ ialah relaksasi fasa (spin-spin); $T_2^{*}$ turut merangkumi kehilangan fasa statik boleh balik yang difokus semula oleh gema Hahn.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A molecule is a set of coupled spins: chemical shift sets each peak's position, and $J$-coupling splits peaks into multiplets following the $n+1$ rule, which together encode chemical environment and connectivity.\n"
msgstr "Molekul ialah set spin berganding: anjakan kimia menentukan kedudukan setiap puncak, dan gandingan $J$ memecahkan puncak menjadi multiplet mengikut peraturan $n+1$, yang bersama-sama mengekod persekitaran kimia dan kesambungan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "True / false {#true-false}"
msgstr "Betul / salah {#true-false}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The Larmor frequency is the energy gap between the two spin states divided by $\\hbar$.\n"
msgstr "B/S Frekuensi Larmor ialah jurang tenaga antara dua keadaan spin dibahagi dengan $\\hbar$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F A $90^\\circ$ ($\\pi/2$) pulse fully inverts an equilibrium spin.\n"
msgstr "B/S Denyut $90^\\circ$ ($\\pi/2$) menyongsangkan sepenuhnya spin keseimbangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F $T_2^{*}$ is generally longer than $T_2$.\n"
msgstr "B/S $T_2^{*}$ umumnya lebih panjang daripada $T_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The Hahn echo refocuses irreversible spin-spin dephasing.\n"
msgstr "B/S Gema Hahn memfokus semula kehilangan fasa spin-spin tak boleh balik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F In an AX$_2$ system the A nucleus appears as a 1:2:1 triplet.\n"
msgstr "B/S Dalam sistem AX$_2$, nukleus A kelihatan sebagai triplet 1:2:1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The coupling constant $J$ doubles when you double the spectrometer's magnetic field.\n"
msgstr "B/S Pemalar gandingan $J$ menjadi dua kali ganda apabila anda menggandakan medan magnet spektrometer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Removing Qiskit Pulse makes it impossible to measure $T_1$ on current hardware.\n"
msgstr "B/S Membuang Qiskit Pulse menjadikan mustahil untuk mengukur $T_1$ pada perkakasan semasa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short answer {#short-answer}"
msgstr "Jawapan pendek {#short-answer}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explain in two sentences why a single $\\pi$ pulse is a poor way to detect a $5\\%$ flip-angle error, and how chaining pulses fixes this.\n"
msgstr "Jelaskan dalam dua ayat mengapa satu denyut $\\pi$ ialah cara yang kurang baik untuk mengesan ralat sudut kilas $5\\%$, dan bagaimana merantai denyut membetulkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A sample shows broad NMR lines. In terms of $T_2$, what does that tell you, and what qubit quantity is the analog?\n"
msgstr "Sampel menunjukkan garis NMR yang lebar. Dari segi $T_2$, apakah yang diberitahu oleh ini, dan apakah kuantiti qubit yang menjadi analognya?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Give the qubit analog of each: (a) the recycle delay, (b) the $90^\\circ$ pulse, (c) the chemical shift.\n"
msgstr "Berikan analog qubit bagi setiap satu: (a) kelewatan kitar semula, (b) denyut $90^\\circ$, (c) anjakan kimia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the $n+1$ rule, explain why an ethyl group (CH$_3$CH$_2$–) shows a 1:2:1 triplet and a 1:3:3:1 quartet, and identify which group produces which multiplet.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan peraturan $n+1$, jelaskan mengapa kumpulan etil (CH$_3$CH$_2$–) menunjukkan triplet 1:2:1 dan kuartet 1:3:3:1, dan kenal pasti kumpulan mana menghasilkan multiplet yang mana.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Challenge problems {#challenge-problems}"
msgstr "Masalah cabaran {#challenge-problems}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Carr-Purcell train.** Modify the Hahn echo to insert $n$ equally spaced $\\pi$ pulses (a CPMG-style train) and measure $T_2$ as a function of $n$. Discuss why more refocusing pulses can lengthen the apparent $T_2$.\n"
msgstr "**Rentetan Carr-Purcell.** Ubah suai gema Hahn untuk menyisipkan $n$ denyut $\\pi$ berjarak sama (rentetan gaya CPMG) dan ukur $T_2$ sebagai fungsi $n$. Bincangkan mengapa lebih banyak denyut pemfokus semula boleh memanjangkan $T_2$ ketara.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pulse-error amplification.** Build a circuit that applies $R_X(\\pi)$ $\\,n$ times to $|0\\rangle$ and plot $P_1$ vs $n$ for a deliberately mis-set angle $R_X(1.05\\pi)$. Show how the error becomes visible as $n$ grows. **Hint:** put a barrier after every rotation; otherwise the transpiler may combine the repeated rotations into a single equivalent gate.\n"
msgstr "**Penguatan ralat denyut.** Bina litar yang mengenakan $R_X(\\pi)$ sebanyak $\\,n$ kali pada $|0\\rangle$ dan plotkan $P_1$ lawan $n$ untuk sudut yang sengaja ditetapkan salah $R_X(1.05\\pi)$. Tunjukkan bagaimana ralat menjadi kelihatan apabila $n$ bertambah. **Petunjuk:** letakkan penghalang selepas setiap putaran; jika tidak, transpiler mungkin menggabungkan putaran berulang itu menjadi satu get setara.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ethyl group.** Using `fid_circuit`, build the proton spectrum of an ethyl fragment (CH$_3$–CH$_2$): five qubits, with the three CH$_3$ protons sharing one chemical shift and the two CH$_2$ protons another, and every CH$_3$–CH$_2$ pair coupled by the same $J$ (no coupling within an equivalent group). Predict the pattern with the $n+1$ rule, then simulate it; you should recover a 1:3:3:1 quartet (CH$_2$) and a 1:2:1 triplet (CH$_3$).\n"
msgstr "**Kumpulan etil.** Menggunakan `fid_circuit`, bina spektrum proton bagi serpihan etil (CH$_3$–CH$_2$): lima qubit, dengan tiga proton CH$_3$ berkongsi satu anjakan kimia dan dua proton CH$_2$ satu lagi, dan setiap pasangan CH$_3$–CH$_2$ berganding dengan $J$ yang sama (tiada gandingan dalam kumpulan setara). Ramalkan coraknya dengan peraturan $n+1$, kemudian simulasikannya; anda sepatutnya mendapat semula kuartet 1:3:3:1 (CH$_2$) dan triplet 1:2:1 (CH$_3$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix (optional): Trotterized evolution — let decoherence set the linewidth {#appendix-optional-trotterized-evolution-let-decoherence-set-the-linewidth}"
msgstr "Lampiran (pilihan): Evolusi Trotter — biarkan dekoheren menentukan lebar garis {#appendix-optional-trotterized-evolution-let-decoherence-set-the-linewidth}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the [NMR spectroscopy of a molecule](#nmr-spectroscopy) section, the evolution $e^{-iHt}$ is applied in a single layer whose depth does **not** grow with $t$, so the FID does not decay on its own and we impose the linewidth with the $e^{-t/T_2}$ apodization window. This optional cell takes the opposite approach. It breaks the evolution into $p$ **Trotter steps** and puts a **barrier** after each step (so the transpiler cannot merge them back into one layer). Time point $k$ uses $k$ steps, so the circuit depth grows with time.\n"
msgstr "Dalam bahagian [Spektroskopi NMR sesebuah molekul](#nmr-spectroscopy), evolusi $e^{-iHt}$ dikenakan dalam satu lapisan yang kedalamannya **tidak** bertambah dengan $t$, jadi FID tidak mereput dengan sendirinya dan kita mengenakan lebar garis dengan tetingkap apodisasi $e^{-t/T_2}$. Sel pilihan ini mengambil pendekatan bertentangan. Ia memecahkan evolusi kepada $p$ **langkah Trotter** dan meletakkan **penghalang** selepas setiap langkah (supaya transpiler tidak boleh menggabungkannya semula menjadi satu lapisan). Titik masa $k$ menggunakan $k$ langkah, jadi kedalaman litar bertambah dengan masa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because every term in $H$ commutes, this is *exact*: on a noiseless simulator it gives the same sharp peaks. But on a **noise-model backend or real hardware** the accumulating gate error makes the FID decay by itself, and that decay is what sets the linewidth. This is the $T_2\\leftrightarrow$linewidth idea of the [$T_2$, $T_2^*$ experiment](#t2t2star) section, now arising from real decoherence instead of a processing window. We run both the **AX** system (two doublets) and the **AX$_2$** system (a 1:2:1 triplet plus a doublet) this way.\n"
msgstr "Kerana setiap sebutan dalam $H$ saling kalis tukar tertib, ini adalah *tepat*: pada simulator tanpa hingar ia memberikan puncak tajam yang sama. Tetapi pada **backend model hingar atau perkakasan sebenar**, ralat get yang terkumpul menyebabkan FID mereput dengan sendirinya, dan pereputan itulah yang menentukan lebar garis. Ini ialah idea $T_2\\leftrightarrow$lebar garis dalam bahagian [eksperimen $T_2$, $T_2^*$](#t2t2star), kini timbul daripada dekoheren sebenar dan bukannya tetingkap pemprosesan. Kita menjalankan kedua-dua sistem **AX** (dua doublet) dan sistem **AX$_2$** (triplet 1:2:1 serta satu doublet) dengan cara ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two practical notes to consider. First, the cost is depth: the deepest AX circuit uses $\\sim\\!47$ two-qubit gates and the AX$_2$ version about twice that, so both are far noisier and more expensive than the exact version. Secondly, each spin system is still submitted as one job, and every time point reuses the same physical-qubit layout selected in the spectroscopy section. If `USE_BATCH=True`, these jobs also use the optional notebook-wide Batch.\n"
msgstr "Dua nota praktikal untuk dipertimbangkan. Pertama, kosnya ialah kedalaman: litar AX terdalam menggunakan $\\sim\\!47$ get dua qubit dan versi AX$_2$ kira-kira dua kali ganda itu, jadi kedua-duanya jauh lebih bising dan lebih mahal daripada versi tepat. Kedua, setiap sistem spin masih dihantar sebagai satu job, dan setiap titik masa menggunakan semula susun atur qubit fizikal yang sama yang dipilih dalam bahagian spektroskopi. Jika `USE_BATCH=True`, job ini turut menggunakan Batch pilihan seluruh buku nota.\n"
